.TH CLOPS_VIDEOS 1 "May 2026" "v2.9.2" "CamClops - Batch Video Generator"
.SH NAME
clops_videos \- batch moving-map, dashboard, and HUD video generator for CamClops trips
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_videos
.I SELECTION
.I TYPE
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.PP
.B "Selection (one or more required):"
.RS
.BI \-\-mid= XX
.RI [ \-\-mid= YY " ...]"
.br
.BI \-\-tid= MM : TT
.RI [ \-\-tid= MM : UU " ...]"
.RE
.PP
.B "Type (one or more required):"
.RS
.B \-\-map
|
.B \-\-dash
|
.B \-\-hud
|
.B \-\-all
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_videos
generates moving-map, instrument dashboard, and HUD overlay videos for one or
more CamClops trips, invoking the appropriate Python rendering scripts and
updating the trip manifest with the output paths on completion.
.PP
It is the command-line equivalent of the
.B Map
/
.B Dashboard
/
.B HUD
generation available in the GUI's Trip Properties dialog, suitable for
unattended batch runs or scripted pipelines.
.PP
Trips are selected by manifest ID
.RB ( \-\-mid ),
trip address
.RB ( \-\-tid ),
or a combination of both.  Multiple flags of each type may be given in one
invocation; the resulting set of (manifest, trip) pairs is deduplicated before
processing.
.PP
For moving-map and HUD generation, GPS track data must be present in the
manifest.
.B clops_videos
attempts GPS extraction automatically if the track is missing; extraction
failure is treated as a warning and the trip is skipped for that video type.
.PP
Output files are written to the footage source directory alongside the
manifest.  Existing output files are skipped unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.SH "SELECTION OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI \-\-mid= XX
Select all trips in manifest
.IR XX .
.I XX
is a two-character manifest ID (case-insensitive; ambiguous characters
normalised:
.BR O\(→0 ,
.BR I\(→1 ,
.BR L\(→1 ).
.TP
.BI \-\-tid= MM : TT
Select the single trip
.I MM:TT
where
.I MM
is the manifest ID and
.I TT
is the trip ID.  Both are case-insensitive.
.SH "TYPE OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-map
Generate a moving-map MP4 via
.IR clops_maprender.py .
GPS track data must be present in the manifest.  Requires Python 3 with
.B Pillow
and
.B requests
installed (for OSM tile fetching).
.TP
.B \-\-dash
Generate an instrument dashboard MP4 via
.IR clops_dashboard.py .
Shows speed, heading, trip odometer, and weather conditions (Open-Meteo
archive API, no API key required).  Requires Python 3 with
.B Pillow
and
.B requests
installed.
.TP
.B \-\-hud
Generate a full-screen HUD overlay WebM via
.IR clops_hud.py .
Output is a VP9/yuva420p transparent WebM suitable for compositing over
collage footage.  Contains left/right speed tapes (KPH/MPH) and a circular
compass rose.  GPS track data must be present.  Requires Python 3 with
.B Pillow
installed.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Equivalent to
.BR "\-\-map \-\-dash \-\-hud" .
.SH "OTHER OPTIONS"
.TP
.B \-\-force
Regenerate output files even if they already exist.  Without this flag,
existing files are silently skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the planned operations without executing any scripts or modifying
any manifests.  Useful for previewing which trips will be processed and
what output paths would be written.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Progress is reported to
.B stdout
as each trip is processed.  Each generated file is listed with its output
path.  Skipped files (already exist, no GPS, or script not found) are noted
with a bracketed reason.
.PP
.nf
[CY:7E]  /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_manifest_CY.json
  map:  /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_trip_7E_map.mp4
  dash: /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_trip_7E_dashboard.mp4
  hud:  /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_trip_7E_hud.webm

[CY:0Y]  /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_manifest_CY.json
  map:  [skip]  /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_trip_0Y_map.mp4
  dash: /z/srcdash/ex10/clops_trip_0Y_dashboard.mp4
  hud:  [no gps]
.fi
.PP
After each trip completes, the manifest is updated with the output paths
.RB ( mapVideos ,
.BR dashVideos ,
.BR hudVideos )
so subsequent tools and the GUI can locate the files without rescanning.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate all three video types for every trip in manifest CY:
.B clops_videos \-\-mid=CY \-\-all
.TP
Generate a map only for one specific trip:
.B clops_videos \-\-tid=CY:7E \-\-map
.TP
Generate maps for two manifests, forcing regeneration:
.B clops_videos \-\-mid=CY \-\-mid=X1 \-\-map \-\-force
.TP
Preview what would run without generating anything:
.B clops_videos \-\-mid=CY \-\-all \-\-dry\-run
.TP
Mix manifest-wide and per-trip selection:
.B clops_videos \-\-mid=CY \-\-tid=X1:3Z \-\-dash \-\-hud
.SH SCRIPTS
.B clops_videos
delegates to the following Python scripts, which must be installed alongside
the binary (or in the system scripts directory):
.TP
.I clops_maprender.py
GPS-synced moving map; fetches OSM tiles; writes MP4.
.TP
.I clops_dashboard.py
Animated instrument panel; fetches weather from Open-Meteo; writes MP4.
.TP
.I clops_hud.py
Transparent HUD overlay; speed tapes and compass rose; writes VP9 WebM.
.PP
Script paths are resolved relative to the
.B clops_videos
binary location, then from the system scripts directory
.RI ( share/camclops/scripts/ ).
If a script is not found, the corresponding video type is skipped for all
trips with a warning to stderr.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All requested videos generated (or skipped as already existing) with no errors.
.TP
.B 1
One or more trips encountered an error (GPS extraction failure, script not
found, or Python error).  Successfully generated files are not rolled back.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/manifests.json
Manifest index used to resolve
.I \-\-mid
and
.I \-\-tid
arguments.
.TP
.I <footage_path>/clops_manifest_<id>.json
Trip manifest.  Updated in-place with output video paths on completion.
.TP
.I <footage_path>/clops_trip_<tid>_map.mp4
Moving-map output (written by
.IR clops_maprender.py ).
.TP
.I <footage_path>/clops_trip_<tid>_dashboard.mp4
Dashboard output (written by
.IR clops_dashboard.py ).
.TP
.I <footage_path>/clops_trip_<tid>_hud.webm
HUD overlay output (written by
.IR clops_hud.py ).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR camclops (1),
.BR clops_gpsinfo (1),
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
.BR clops_ls (1)
